Gemmified-gm-recomp
===================

A fork of gm-recomp <https://github.com/KurathSec/gm-recomp> that packages it as
a plugin for hosts that speak the GEMS plugin protocol.

It is based on upstream commit 9d38d083de3691288ebea49f57da6225e3b58f26
(2026-10-27). Upstream commits after that one are not included.

gm-recomp is licensed MIT and so is this fork; see LICENSE. Copyright in the
original work is retained by KurathSec. Modifications in this fork, including
host/ and scripts/, are Copyright (c) 2026 Dapper Mink, under the same MIT
licence (host/gems/LICENSE repeats it for that directory).

This fork removes upstream's crates/gmmod (game-file patching tooling, which
carried encodings derived from UndertaleModLib, GPL-3.0, with no licence note)
and everything that used it, so no UndertaleModLib-derived code is in this
repository or its builds.

Third-party components
----------------------

Wine DLLs. The plugin build carries, in system32/, 32-bit DLLs from WineHQ's
own build of Wine 11.0 <https://www.winehq.org/>: the redistributable runtimes
(C/C++ runtimes, the shader compiler, D3DX 9, msacm32, and what they import)
that games call but do not ship. They are not in this repository:
scripts/system32.sh downloads WineHQ's package, checks its sha256, and strips
the DLLs' debug sections. They are licensed LGPL-2.1-or-later, and the runtime
loads them as separate files, like a game's own DLLs. Wine's licence
(COPYING.LIB), its copyright notice (LICENSE) and a README saying where the
source is go beside them in system32/. Their source, wine-11.0.tar.xz, is
published beside each release, at
https://gemmified-gm-recomp.dappermink.me/<version>/wine-11.0.tar.xz, and is
also at https://dl.winehq.org/wine/source/11.0/wine-11.0.tar.xz.

Rust crates linked into the browser runtime (web.wasm), whose licences are not
MIT or MIT/Apache-2.0:
  - symphonia (MP3 decoding): MPL-2.0, file-level copyleft; its source is at
    <https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia> and on crates.io.
  - rustc_apfloat: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception.
  - encoding_rs: (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) AND BSD-3-Clause.
